{# A page's title and the line under it.

   For a page that is neither prose nor a directory. Those two carry their own
   header inside their sheet -- see partials/article.html.twig and
   partials/directory.html.twig -- and a page with cards under it has nowhere
   to put one, so it had been borrowing Bootstrap's `display-4` and `.lead`.
   That rendered 56px at weight 300 where every other title in the app is 28 to
   32px at 700: the largest and lightest heading on the site, on the only two
   pages that had not been given one of their own.

   The type is the directory's, because these pages are its kin -- a title, a
   line saying what the list is, and then the list. #}
<header class="page-head">
    <h1 class="page-head__title">{{ title }}</h1>
    {% if lead is defined and lead is not empty %}
        <p class="page-head__lead">{{ lead }}</p>
    {% endif %}
</header>
